#, no-c-format
msgid "Frequently asked questions"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:294
#, no-c-format
msgid "Who made this game?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:295
#, no-c-format
msgid "The kdegames team. You can find their website here."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:298
#, no-c-format
msgid "Where can I get cheatcodes?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:299
#, no-c-format
msgid "You can't get cheatcodes for KDE games."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:302
#, no-c-format
msgid "How do I know what does the molecule look like?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:303
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can view the molecule on the reference screen located in the top right "
"corner of the game screen."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:306
#, no-c-format
msgid "Where is the reference screen?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:307
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The reference screen is located in the top right corner of the game screen."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:310
#, no-c-format
msgid "How do I move a game piece(atom)?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:311
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To move a game piece(atom) use your mouse cursor to click on it. At this "
"time the available directional icon will become visible. Click on the "
"corresponding directional icon to make a game piece move in desired "
"direction. Alternatively, you can use your keyboard to move the pieces. Use "
"[Tab] key to switch between the items, and directional key to move them once "
"selected."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:314
#, no-c-format
msgid "Can I use keyboard to control the pieces(atoms)?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:315
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Yes. Use [Tab] key to switch between the items, and directional key to move "
"them once selected."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:318
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When I move a peace (atom) it goes right past the place where I want it. How "
"do I make it stop there?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:319
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You don't. Once an atom begins moving, it will not stop until it meets "
"either a wall or another peace."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:322
#, no-c-format
msgid "I have stuck. How can I restart the game?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:323
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To restart Karomic choose 'Game' in the game window menu. There choose "
"'Restart Game'. Alternatively you can press [F5] key on your keyboard to "
"restart the game."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:326
#, no-c-format
msgid "I can't beat the level. Is there a hint system, or a solver?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:327
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"No. Unfortunately at this time Katomic does not feature a hint system. So "
"the only way to finish a level is to solve it on your own."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:330
#, no-c-format
msgid "I did something wrong. Can I undo."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:331
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Yes. To undo a wrong move select 'Move' from the menubar. Then select "
"'Undo'. Alternatively you can press [Ctrl+Z] on your keyboard."
msgstr ""

